cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QFactor-Penny, please cite this software artifact."
type: software
title: "QFactor-Penny: A Reproducible Benchmark of Trainable Quantum Circuits for Cross-Sectional Sector Return Ranking"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-13"
authors:
  - family-names: "Mahashin"
    given-names: "Tazeem"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Taz33m/qfactor-penny"
url: "https://github.com/Taz33m/qfactor-penny"
license: "MIT"
abstract: "QFactor-Penny is a leakage-aware PennyLane and Qiskit benchmark for trainable quantum circuits in cross-sectional sector ETF ranking. It compares small QNNs against classical baselines, audits leakage and feature stability, documents QNN constant-score collapse, and includes an optional IBM Quantum System One hardware robustness audit without claiming quantum advantage or trading edge."
keywords:
  - "quantum machine learning"
  - "PennyLane"
  - "Qiskit"
  - "quantitative finance"
  - "walk-forward validation"
  - "sector ETF ranking"
  - "failure-mode benchmark"
